dm's change to librqbit-sha1-wrapper 9.1.0 (crates.io, Apache-2.0), applied
to the published crate with Cargo.lock, Cargo.toml.orig, .cargo_vcs_info.json
and .cargo-ok removed first. Made again by `cargo xtask vendor`; explained
in desktop/vendor/README.md (each change marked `dm(sha1):`, its row in that
file's table). The text before each file's section says what its hunks do, in
order; git apply skips it.

Cargo.toml:
  1. The feature `sha1-ring`, the name librqbit and librqbit-core ask for, is
     backed by the pure-Rust sha1 and sha2 crates rather than aws-lc-rs (a
     second crypto library, in C, built with cmake; gaps row P7).
  2. The sha1 and sha2 dependencies in place of aws-lc-rs.

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 4f59e97..e1a8cc4 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -29,7 +29,10 @@ resolver = "2"
 [features]
 default = ["sha1-crypto-hash"]
 sha1-crypto-hash = ["crypto-hash"]
-sha1-ring = ["aws-lc-rs"]
+# dm(sha1): the name librqbit-core and librqbit ask for, kept, now backed by the
+# pure-Rust sha1 and sha2 crates rather than aws-lc-rs, which built a second
+# crypto library in C (with cmake) beside ring (desktop/vendor/README.md).
+sha1-ring = ["sha1", "sha2"]
 
 [lib]
 name = "librqbit_sha1_wrapper"
@@ -38,9 +41,15 @@ path = "src/lib.rs"
 [dependencies.assert_cfg]
 version = "0.1"
 
-[dependencies.aws-lc-rs]
-version = "1.12"
+[dependencies.sha1]
+version = "0.11"
 optional = true
+default-features = false
+
+[dependencies.sha2]
+version = "0.11"
+optional = true
+default-features = false
 
 [dependencies.crypto-hash]
 version = "0.3"
src/lib.rs:
  1-3. `Sha1Ring` and `Sha256Ring` over sha1::Sha1 and sha2::Sha256 (the
     names are upstream's, which librqbit uses).
  4. A test of the FIPS 180 "abc" vector for SHA-1, fed in two parts.

